<title>GERMANY: Krupp workers halt production to protest cuts.</title>
<headline>Krupp workers halt production to protest cuts.</headline>
<dateline>DORTMUND, Germany 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>More than 1,000 workers at a Krupp Hoesch Stahl AG steel plant halted production on Wednesday morning to protest a management reorganisation plan, union represntatives said.</p>
<p>The workers, who planned a 24-hour work stoppage, hoped to push the Krupp supervisory board to reject the plan to eliminate about 2,200 of the company's 10,000 jobs.</p>
<p>The supervisory board was expected to consider the plan at a Wednesday afternoon meeting. Workers want Krupp to invest in modern equipment at the Dortmund plant to preserve the jobs.</p>
<p>Workers from a Bochum plant planned drive more than 300 cars to Dortmund to join the protest.</p>
<p>Krupp is the steel unit of Fried. Krupp AG Hoesch-Krupp.</p>
